<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22145" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηροβοσκ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to feed</i> or <i>cherish in old age</i>, esp.
			one's parents, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1033
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alc.</u>
				663
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demoph.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					43
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be cherished when old</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				678
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηρωβοσκήσει</span> is read in
				<i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				49.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηρωβοσκήσαντα</span> is
				v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				3.1.38
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηρο-κομεῖον, -κομέω, -κομία,
				-κόμος</span>: such forms might be due to 
				contr.
			 of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηραο-</span>, but are more
			prob. misspellings).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>